{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-minor-offnet-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.74, step 7f. `scale-county-minor-offnet`: the PM species and the PAH particles at the OFF-NETWORK exhaust processes, NOT aggregated -- start exhaust (2), extended idle (90), APU (91), crankcase start (16) and crankcase extended idle (17), for source types 21 and 62 on road type 1 alone, over the county database `inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`, at `<aggregateBy key=\"Hour\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Hour\"/>`: July 2020, weekdays, hour 8. It selects PM10 and PM2.5 totals (100, 110), organic and elemental carbon (111, 112), sulfate (115), NonECPM (118), aerosol water (119), nitrate and ammonium (35, 36), the PM2.5 elements chloride to iron (51-59), PMOTHR, NCOM, TOM and the residual (121-124) and the PAH particles (23, 68-78, 81-84) at each. MOVESOutput is 17,062 rows: 38 pollutants at start and crankcase start (154 each), extended idle and crankcase extended idle (50) and APU (41). Its running-exhaust half is `scale-county-minor-running`; the two were one capture of all seven processes (75,582 rows) that the evaluation could not hold in memory. Its Year twin is `scale-county-timeagg-year-minor-offnet`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES: SulfatePMCalculator's pmSpeciation outputs beyond organic carbon (nitrate, ammonium, the elements, PMOTHR, NCOM) and its two sums of them (TOM = OC + NCOM, the residual = the residue times one minus their fractions); its crankcase split, which writes crankcase start's and crankcase extended idle's PM from START's and EXTENDED IDLE's species times `crankcaseEmissionRatio` at the crankcase process, reading `sulfateFractions` and the residue's fuel ratio at the parent; and AirToxicsCalculator's PAH particles from organic carbon at the SAME process (`pahParticleRatio`), crankcase ones included. Before PLAN.md §7.3.74 the model wrote none of the 13 new species or 16 particles and no crankcase PM, and counted nothing (`run_selectionUnported` 0).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 17062, the (pollutant-process, cohort) rows of the one (county, month, hour cell); `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "start-exhaust",
      "crankcase",
      "pm-speciation",
      "air-toxics"
    ]
  },
